WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:17.706
Two members of the submarine's crew helped us to dress for our underwater walk.

2
00:00:17.707 --> 00:00:23.874
Our diving suits were made of heavy rubber and constructed to resist the great pressure of the water.

3
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:30.358
Each suit consisted of a jacket and trousers joined together with bands of copper crossing the chest.

4
00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:34.525
The sleeves ended in gloves that allowed the fingers to move easily.

5
00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:39.200
The trousers were finished off with thick boots weighted with heavy lead.

6
00:00:39.201 --> 00:00:44.113
Captain Nemo, one of his crew, Conseil, and I were soon dressed.

7
00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:50.113
The upper part of the diving suit ended in a copper collar upon which was screwed a metal helmet.

8
00:00:50.114 --> 00:00:55.517
Three holes, protected by thick glass, allowed us to see in all directions.

9
00:00:55.518 --> 00:01:01.097
I was relieved to find that I could breathe with ease once the apparatus was turned on.

10
00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:04.938
Our diving suits were so heavy that it was difficult to walk.

11
00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:09.526
Fortunately we only had to take a few steps into another small room.

12
00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:14.597
Then the door closed and we were wrapped in profound darkness.

13
00:01:14.598 --> 00:01:23.994
After a few minutes, I heard a loud hissing and felt cold rising from my feet to my chest. Evidently water was entering the room.

14
00:01:23.995 --> 00:01:30.828
When the room was full of water, another door opened in the side of the submarine and we stepped onto the sea bottom!

15
00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:40.478
How can I explain what it was like to walk underwater? Mere words are insufficient. I was astonished by how bright it was.

16
00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:47.224
Would you believe me if I said that at a depth of thirty feet I could see as if in broad daylight?

17
00:01:47.225 --> 00:02:00.048
The sun's rays touched flowers, rocks, plants, and shells, providing a perfect kaleidoscope of colors: red, green, yellow, orange, purple, and blue.

18
00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:05.723
I wanted to share my amazement with Conseil, but underwater there was no way to communicate with him.

19
00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:10.707
Soon the nature of the soil changed from sand to slimy mud.

20
00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:16.866
Then we traveled over a plain of algae that was as soft as any carpet woven by man.

21
00:02:16.867 --> 00:02:25.858
After a while the ground began to slope downward. The colors were no longer as brilliant, but we had no need of our lights yet.

22
00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:31.691
When we reached a depth of about three hundred feet, Captain Nemo signaled for us to stop.

23
00:02:31.692 --> 00:02:35.771
He pointed to a dark mass looming in the shadows.

24
00:02:35.772 --> 00:02:41.009
"This must be the forest of Crespo," I thought and I was right.

25
00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:46.921
As the captain had said, the forest was underwater. There was no sign of an island.

26
00:02:46.922 --> 00:02:50.342
Captain Nemo regarded this forest as his own.

27
00:02:50.343 --> 00:02:54.517
And who would have challenged his possession of this underwater real estate?

28
00:02:54.518 --> 00:03:00.326
What other pioneer would come, hatchet in hand, to cut down these dark masses of plant life?

29
00:03:00.327 --> 00:03:04.588
The forest was composed of large plants that resembled trees.

30
00:03:04.589 --> 00:03:10.818
I was struck by the unusual position of their branches, something that I had never observed before.

31
00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:16.739
No herb that carpeted the ground or branch that adorned a tree extended horizontally.

32
00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:21.905
They all stretched up to the surface of the ocean as straight as iron bars.

33
00:03:21.906 --> 00:03:27.802
I soon grew used to this strange fact as well as to the growing darkness that surrounded us.

34
00:03:27.803 --> 00:03:35.802
The soil of the forest was covered with sharp rocks that were difficult to avoid, and it was hard to tell the plants from the animals.

35
00:03:35.803 --> 00:03:45.040
It was still impossible to speak and be heard, so I put my great copper head next to Conseil's. His eyes were shining with delight.

36
00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:50.873
After a couple hours of walking underwater, I was surprised that I wasn't terribly hungry.

37
00:03:50.874 --> 00:03:59.444
Instead I felt an overwhelming desire to sleep, something that happens to all divers. We all stretched out for a nap.

38
00:03:59.445 --> 00:04:05.198
I don't know how long I stayed asleep, but when I awoke, Captain Nemo had already risen.

39
00:04:05.199 --> 00:04:10.445
I was starting to stretch my limbs when something startled me and I jumped to my feet.

40
00:04:10.446 --> 00:04:20.349
A few steps away a giant sea spider, thirty-eight inches high, was watching me and was ready to spring.

41
00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:26.349
Although my diving suit was thick enough to protect me from this animal, I couldn't help shuddering with horror.

42
00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:33.833
At this moment Conseil and the other sailor from the Nautilus awoke, and Captain Nemo pointed out the hideous crustacean.

43
00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:38.516
He knocked the creature over with his gun, and I saw its horrible claws.

44
00:04:38.517 --> 00:04:46.254
This incident made me aware that we might encounter even more fearful animals—creatures whose attacks might penetrate my diving suit.

45
00:04:46.255 --> 00:04:50.254
I hadn't thought of this before, but I resolved to be on my guard.

46
00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:55.659
I was sure that our resting spot would mark the end of our walk, but Captain Nemo pressed on.

47
00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:02.984
We continued going downhill until we reached a depth of 450 feet and it got very dark.

48
00:05:02.985 --> 00:05:11.389
I had no instruments to measure this depth, but I knew that the sun's rays couldn't penetrate even the clearest water at 450 feet.

49
00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:14.722
We turned on our lights and could see ahead of us.

50
00:05:14.723 --> 00:05:21.555
Captain Nemo kept plunging into the depths of the forest, whose trees were getting scarcer at every step.

51
00:05:21.556 --> 00:05:26.127
I was sure that our lights would draw some deep-sea dweller from its dark bed.

52
00:05:26.128 --> 00:05:30.468
But if sea creatures did approach us, they kept a respectful distance.

53
00:05:30.469 --> 00:05:36.539
Several times Captain Nemo raised his gun to his shoulder, but then dropped it and walked on.

54
00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:43.356
At last this marvelous excursion came to an end when we reached a wall of solid rock.

55
00:05:43.357 --> 00:05:51.277
There was no way to climb it. We had reached the base of the island of Crespo, and Captain Nemo would not venture onto land.

56
00:05:51.278 --> 00:05:55.023
We returned home by a different, steeper route.

57
00:05:55.024 --> 00:06:02.420
As we reached shallower waters, the captain shot a sea otter and his companion brought down a bird that was hovering above the waves.

58
00:06:02.421 --> 00:06:08.594
Off in the distance I spotted the bright light from the Nautilus; we would be onboard in less than twenty minutes.

59
00:06:08.595 --> 00:06:12.769
I could tell that my air supply was beginning to run low on oxygen.

60
00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:19.920
Suddenly Captain Nemo rushed toward me and pushed me to the ground. His companion did the same thing to Conseil.

61
00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:27.174
I didn't know what to think of this unexpected attack, but I was reassured by seeing the captain lie down beside me and remain motionless.

62
00:06:27.175 --> 00:06:35.332
I was stretched on the ground just under the shelter of an algae bush when I saw an enormous mass glide overhead.

63
00:06:35.333 --> 00:06:41.578
My blood froze in my veins as I recognized two giant sharks passing over us.

64
00:06:41.579 --> 00:06:48.554
They were blue sharks—an especially fierce kind of shark that could crush a man with their iron jaws!

65
00:06:48.555 --> 00:06:52.475
Happily for us, these hungry creatures couldn't see well.

66
00:06:52.476 --> 00:06:57.229
They passed without spotting us even though they brushed us with their fins.

67
00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:03.118
By some miracle, we managed to escape a danger greater than meeting a tiger face-to-face!

68
00:07:03.119 --> 00:07:06.380
In a few minutes, we were back at the Nautilus.

69
00:07:06.381 --> 00:07:10.697
I don't know whether Conseil had classified the sharks as they swam over us.

70
00:07:10.698 --> 00:07:18.119
All I know is that I had observed them more as a potential victim than as a naturalist.
